<article class="bueno"><header><div class="meta case-meta"><span class="case-meta__client-full">Taco Bueno Restaurants</span><span class="case-meta__client-short">Taco Bueno</span><span class="case-meta__highlight">+147% engagement</span><span class="case-meta__role">Senior UX Strategist &amp; Creative Lead</span></div><div class="intro"><div><p>Brand Strategy &amp; Integrated Campaign UX</p><h1>Bueno<br />Means<br /><span class="heading-accent">Better.</span></h1></div><p>Taco Bueno's marketing increasingly resembled its competitors despite its fresh-daily preparation.</p></div></header>
  <CaseContents links={[{"href": "#case-section-1", "label": "Research"}, {"href": "#case-section-2", "label": "Brand platform"}, {"href": "#case-section-3", "label": "Campaign"}, {"href": "#case-section-4", "label": "Results"}]} /><figure class="hero"><img src="/images/taco_bueno_intro.webp" alt="Taco Bueno restaurant mural and interior concept" loading="eager" decoding="async" /></figure>
<section class="bueno-detail" aria-labelledby="bueno-brief"><div><p class="bueno-detail__label">The brief</p><h2 id="bueno-brief">Find the story customers already believed.</h2></div><div class="bueno-detail__copy"><p>As Senior UX Strategist and Creative Lead through Pocket Made, I led the positioning, messaging, and digital UX for Bueno Means Better, connecting the website, microsite, social, email, outdoor, and restaurant experience.</p></div></section>
<section class="research" id="case-section-1" tabindex="-1"><div><p>01 / The insight</p><h2>Research &amp; Brand<br />Differentiation</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>An audit of three years of marketing and six regional quick-service and fast-casual competitors found recurring campaign-language similarities.</p><p>In moderated sessions with eighteen current and lapsed customers across three Southwest markets, current customers valued freshness and made-from-scratch preparation; lapsed customers described an interchangeable brand.</p></div><figure class="research__wide"><img src="/images/taco_bueno01.webp" alt="Taco Bueno campaign system across OOH and digital" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure></section>
<section class="proof" id="case-section-2" tabindex="-1"><div class="proof__head"><p>02 / The platform</p><h2>Freshness was the<br /><span class="heading-accent">proof point.</span></h2></div><div class="copy"><p>I centered the messaging on kitchen details, with shared guidance for humor, honesty, and appetite appeal.</p><p>Different formats returned to the same preparation story rather than starting a new theme in each channel.</p></div><div class="proof__art"><figure><img src="/images/taco_bueno02.webp" alt="Taco Bueno storefront graphics" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure><figure><img src="/images/taco_bueno03.webp" alt="Taco Bueno billboards featuring fresh food messaging" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure></div></section>
<section class="digital" id="case-section-3" tabindex="-1"><div><p>03 / Show the work</p><h2><span class="digital-title-line">Show the</span><span class="digital-title-line">Preparation.</span><span class="digital-title-line">Invite Participation.</span></h2></div><figure><img src="/images/taco_bueno04-1.webp" alt="The Bean Cam shown as a live digital billboard" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure><div class="copy"><p>Customer sessions and secondary research on kitchen transparency informed Bean Cam: a live stream showing beans being made to support the campaign promise.</p><p>Conversational email carried the voice, while Snapchat's #Shellfies invited customers to contribute their taco experiences.</p></div><figure class="shellfies"><img src="/images/taco_bueno05.webp" alt="Shellfies user-generated Taco Bueno social campaign" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure></section>
<section class="bueno-detail" aria-labelledby="bueno-physical"><div><p class="bueno-detail__label">Outdoor &amp; in-store</p><h2 id="bueno-physical">Carry the preparation story to the counter.</h2></div><div class="bueno-detail__copy"><p>Outdoor concepts included a time-stamped first batch of guacamole, giving freshness a specific example.</p><p>Bold type and texture extended the language into menu boards and promotional cards; Pocket Made's creative team collaborated on outdoor and print production from my strategic direction and voice guidelines.</p></div></section>
<section class="results" id="case-section-4" tabindex="-1"><div><p>04 / Results</p><h2>Results &amp;<br />Market Performance</h2></div><div class="numbers"><div><b>147%</b><span>increase in social engagement</span></div><div><b>3%</b><span>increase in average check</span></div><div><b>12</b><span>pilot restaurants</span></div></div><div class="copy"><p>The original project account reports 147% higher social engagement than the previous campaign and a 3% average-check increase across twelve pilot restaurants during the campaign period. These campaign-level figures do not isolate any UX or creative decision.</p><p>The account also describes improved freshness, authenticity, and made-from-scratch perceptions across the three test markets, without the survey detail needed to quantify that change here.</p></div></section><section class="bueno-detail" aria-labelledby="bueno-reflection"><div><p class="bueno-detail__label">Reflection</p><h2 id="bueno-reflection">Define how the pilot should inform a wider rollout.</h2></div><div class="bueno-detail__copy"><p>I would define expansion criteria before pilot results arrived, specifying measures, comparison periods, and operational requirements for a phased rollout.</p><p>That would give the team a basis for deciding what to retain, adapt, or test beyond the twelve restaurants.</p></div></section></article>
